---
import DocPageLayout from "../../layouts/DocPageLayout.astro";
---

<DocPageLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="Run a test-backed LiteMCP governed-endpoint proof locally, then inspect the demo control plane without relying on a hosted account."
  currentPath="/docs/getting-started"
>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Development status</strong>
    <p>
      LiteMCP Composer is pre-1.0. The proof below uses an ephemeral loopback server, in-memory
      data, sandbox tools, and a fixed demo identity. It is product evidence—not production,
      identity-provider, named-client, or deployment acceptance.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Node.js 22.12 or newer</li>
    <li>pnpm 10.30.2</li>
    <li>No Docker, hosted account, private package, or external MCP server for the local proof</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="install">Install the workspace</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/reachjalil/liteMCP.git
cd liteMCP
corepack enable
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile</code></pre>

  <h2 id="five-minute-proof">Run the five-minute governed-endpoint proof</h2>
  <pre><code>pnpm demo:smoke</code></pre>
  <p>
    One command reserves a loopback port, starts the portable Node composition in explicit demo
    mode, executes the SDK scenario against real HTTP and MCP routes, and stops the server. A
    successful run ends with:
  </p>
  <pre><code>PASS real loopback MCP initialize and filtered discovery
PASS builtin and remote governed tool execution
PASS hidden denial and exact-context approval pause/resume
PASS payload-free activation and redacted audit evidence
PASS revoked session denied at the gateway boundary</code></pre>

  <h3 id="proof-scenario">What the scenario exercises</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>An employee session initializes MCP and receives a policy-filtered tool catalog.</li>
    <li><code>finance.issue_refund</code> is hidden, and a guessed direct call is denied before upstream dispatch.</li>
    <li>Allowed built-in and remote tools execute, including a sandbox sum that returns <code>42</code>.</li>
    <li>A finance session can discover the refund tool, but execution pauses for an exact-context approval.</li>
    <li>A separate local demo administrator approves the request; one identical retry succeeds and consumes the approval.</li>
    <li>Revocation blocks the employee session, while audit and activation records exclude the tested token, account ID, and refund reason.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Proof boundary</strong>
    <p>
      This validates the maintained local vertical slice. It does not establish production
      hardening, broad MCP-client compatibility, live OIDC/SAML/SCIM behavior, upstream OAuth
      brokering, Kubernetes runtime behavior, backup/restore, managed-cloud availability, an
      external security review, or a compliance posture.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="interactive-demo">Explore the local control plane</h2>
  <pre><code>LITEMCP_DEMO_MODE=true pnpm dev</code></pre>
  <p>
    The web surface defaults to <code>http://localhost:4321</code> and the management API to
    <code>http://localhost:8787</code>. The root command starts only the portable Node server and
    Astro site; it does not start or authenticate against the managed-cloud runtime.
  </p>
  <p>
    With the command running, open the
    <a href="http://localhost:4321/app?demo=1">local demo console</a>. Do not expose demo mode to a
    shared network or treat its fixed identity as an authentication test.
  </p>

  <h3 id="inspect-api">Inspect the demo tenant directly</h3>
  <pre><code>curl --fail-with-body http://localhost:8787/api/v1/overview \
  -H 'x-litemcp-tenant: org_demo' \
  -H 'x-litemcp-role: finance-admin'</code></pre>
  <p>
    Those headers are accepted only in explicit demo mode. Production requests must derive the
    tenant, membership, actor, roles, and authorization state from a trusted authenticated server
    session.
  </p>

  <h2 id="next">Choose the next evidence step</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Inspect the <a href="/security">security and evidence boundaries</a>.</li>
    <li>Review the <a href="/docs/self-hosting">self-hosting assets and pending runtime proof</a>.</li>
    <li>Read the <a href="https://github.com/reachjalil/liteMCP/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md">implementation evidence and acceptance gaps</a>.</li>
    <li>If the local slice matches a real high-risk workflow, <a href="/design-partners">qualify a design-partner pilot</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</DocPageLayout>
